<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds closed at session highs, buoyed by news from Dublin that the European Union had agreed on terms of a stability pact to ensure fiscal discipline after monetary union.</p>
<p>Traders said they saw the spread with the bunds in the 10-year cash, which dropped to a historical low of 110 basis points, remaining around this level or even narrowing further towards 100.</p>
<p>The greater liquidity of the Spanish market would wipe out the negative spread that had previously existed with bonos, they added. --Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
